                <pb facs="0560" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13887: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-11T15:00:00+08:00">January 11, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 11—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Information has been received from local office of the Eurasia Aviation
                    Corporation that their plane No. 18 left Sian this morning at 11 a.m. with 16
                    foreigners on board en route to Shanghai. It is understood that evacuation was
                    made under arrangements by Chinese authorities in Nanking. Identity of
                    foreigners being evacuated unknown.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking; by mail to Peiping and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
